Logistics Optimization Crew AI System
Overview
The Logistics Optimization Crew AI System is a Streamlit-based application designed to analyze logistics operations and provide actionable optimization strategies for delivery routes and inventory management. Tailored for the Indian market, it uses Indian Rupees (₹) for all monetary values and accounts for regional factors like monsoon seasons and festival periods. The system leverages AI agents powered by the Groq API to analyze user-uploaded data and generate insights.
This repository contains two main scripts:

logistics_optimization_crew.py: A Streamlit app that allows users to upload logistics data, visualize key performance metrics, and run AI-driven optimization analysis.
generate_data_templates.py: A utility script to generate CSV templates for delivery and inventory data, along with detailed documentation to guide users in preparing their data.

Features

Data Upload: Upload delivery and inventory data in CSV format for analysis.
Dashboard: Visualize key logistics metrics (e.g., average delivery time, on-time rate, fuel costs in ₹, total packages).
AI Analysis: Two AI agents (Logistics Analyst and Optimization Strategist) analyze data and provide optimization recommendations.
Indian Context: Supports Indian Rupees (₹) and considers regional factors like traffic, weather, and festival seasons.
Data Templates: Generate pre-formatted CSV templates to ensure data compatibility with the Streamlit app.
Export Options: Download analysis results as a JSON report (PDF generation is a placeholder feature).

Prerequisites

Python: Version 3.8 or higher
Dependencies: Install required Python packages using:pip install streamlit pandas numpy plotly groq


Groq API Key: Obtain a free API key from https://console.groq.com/keys to enable AI analysis.
Spreadsheet Editor: Software like Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets to edit CSV templates.

Installation

Clone this repository:git clone <repository-url>
cd <repository-directory>


Install dependencies:pip install -r requirements.txt

If a requirements.txt file is not provided, install the required packages listed above.
Ensure you have a valid Groq API key.

Usage
Step 1: Generate Data Templates
The generate_data_templates.py script creates CSV templates and documentation for preparing your logistics data.

Run the script:
python generate_data_templates.py


This generates three files:

delivery_data_template.csv: Template for delivery data.
inventory_data_template.csv: Template for inventory data.
DATA_TEMPLATE_GUIDE.md: Detailed documentation on required and optional fields.


Open the CSV templates in a spreadsheet editor (e.g., Excel, Google Sheets).

Replace the sample data with your actual logistics data, ensuring all required fields are included:

Delivery Data:
date: YYYY-MM-DD format (e.g., 2024-01-15)
route_id: Unique route identifier (e.g., MUM_001)
delivery_time_hours: Delivery time in hours (e.g., 4.5)
distance_km: Distance in kilometers (e.g., 120)
fuel_cost_inr: Fuel cost in Indian Rupees (e.g., 1200)
packages_delivered: Number of packages (e.g., 25)
on_time_delivery: Boolean (True/False or 1/0)


Inventory Data:
product_id: Unique product identifier (e.g., PROD_001)
current_stock: Current stock level (e.g., 150)
reorder_point: Minimum stock before reordering (e.g., 100)
holding_cost_per_unit_inr: Holding cost per unit in ₹ (e.g., 12.50)
demand_last_30_days: Demand in last 30 days (e.g., 85)
supplier_lead_time_days: Supplier delivery time in days (e.g., 7)




Save the files as CSV format.


Step 2: Run the Streamlit App
The logistics_optimization_crew.py script runs the Streamlit app for data analysis and optimization.

Start the Streamlit app:streamlit run logistics_optimization_crew.py


Open the app in your browser (typically at http://localhost:8501).
In the sidebar:
Enter your Groq API key.
Upload the filled delivery_data_template.csv and inventory_data_template.csv files.


If the uploaded files pass validation, the app will display a dashboard with key metrics.
Click Start Analysis to run the AI-driven optimization process.
View results in the tabs: Analysis Results, Optimization Strategy, and Implementation Plan.
Download the JSON report or (optionally) generate a PDF report (placeholder feature).

Data Requirements

Delivery Data:
Must include all required columns listed above.
Optional fields (e.g., driver_id, vehicle_type, start_city) can enhance analysis but are not mandatory.


Inventory Data:
Must include all required columns listed above.
Optional fields (e.g., product_name, supplier_city) improve analysis quality.


Data Quality:
Use YYYY-MM-DD for dates.
Ensure numerical fields (e.g., fuel_cost_inr, distance_km) are positive and realistic.
Use consistent naming for text fields (e.g., MUM_001 for route IDs).
Use True/False or 1/0 for boolean fields.


Sample Size:
Minimum: 100 delivery records, 50 inventory items.
Recommended: 500+ delivery records, 100+ inventory items for robust analysis.



Indian Market Considerations

Currency: All costs (e.g., fuel_cost_inr, holding_cost_per_unit_inr) are in Indian Rupees (₹).
Regional Factors:
Monsoon seasons (June-September) may affect delivery times.
Festival periods (e.g., Diwali, Durga Puja) can cause traffic and demand spikes.
Regional variations (e.g., North India traffic, South India port access) are considered in the templates.


Cost Factors:
Fuel prices vary by state (~₹100-110/liter).
Toll charges and labor costs differ across regions.



Files in the Repository

logistics_optimization_crew.py: Main Streamlit app for logistics analysis and optimization.
generate_data_templates.py: Script to generate data templates and documentation.
delivery_data_template.csv: Generated template for delivery data (after running generate_data_templates.py).
inventory_data_template.csv: Generated template for inventory data.
DATA_TEMPLATE_GUIDE.md: Documentation for data templates, including field descriptions and guidelines.

Limitations

AI Data Integration: The current AI tasks do not directly process uploaded data. To enhance analysis, modify the execute_task method in logistics_optimization_crew.py to include data summaries in the Groq API prompts.
PDF Generation: The "Generate PDF Report" feature is a placeholder and requires implementation (e.g., using reportlab or weasyprint).
Data Validation: The app checks for required columns but does not validate data types or ranges. Add further validation if needed (e.g., ensuring delivery_time_hours is numeric).

Future Enhancements

Integrate uploaded data into AI prompts for more relevant analysis.
Implement PDF report generation.
Add advanced data validation (e.g., type checking, range validation).
Support for scheduling periodic analyses.
Include predictive modeling for demand forecasting.

Troubleshooting

Validation Errors: If you see errors like "Delivery data must contain columns...", ensure your CSV files include all required columns exactly as specified (e.g., fuel_cost_inr instead of fuel_cost).
API Errors: Verify your Groq API key is valid and you have sufficient quota. Visit https://console.groq.com/keys for details.
CSV Issues: Ensure CSV files are properly formatted (e.g., no missing headers, no special characters in numerical fields).

